{"metadata":{"description":"Local-first SSH host & credential manager for humans and AI agents — OS-keychain vault, loopback web UI, one-line Agent Skill deploy","id":"gh:1301955783","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"hoploom","slug":"xiayh0107/hoploom","topics":["agent-context","agent-plugins","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Local-first SSH host & credential manager for humans and AI agents — OS-keychain vault, loopback web"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" UI, one-line Agent Skill deploy"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Hoploom"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> **A local-first secure server access layer for humans and AI agents.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Manage SSH hosts, credentials, remote access, and host-specific agent context from one deterministic"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" interface — without putting secrets in config files, shell history, or an AI model's context."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Website · Documentation · Product README · 简体中文"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Previously **SSH Server Manager** / `servers-connect`. Existing `serverctl`
commands remain compatib"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"le; follow the upgrade guide
to migrate an existing installation without changing its data or vault "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"ow the upgrade guide
to migrate an existing installation without changing its data or vault entries."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Why Hoploom?"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"OpenSSH is excellent at transport. The hard part is everything around it:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- remembering which hostname, user, port, bastion, or credential belongs to which machine;
- keeping"},{"id":"p9s2","text":" passwords and key passphrases out of dotfiles, scripts, environment variables, and shell history;
-"},{"id":"p9s3","text":" letting coding agents operate remote machines without exposing credentials to the model;
- keeping "},{"id":"p9s4","text":"environment-specific procedures attached to the hosts where they actually apply;
- providing one con"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"sistent interface across macOS, Linux, and Windows."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"`Hoploom` puts a small local control layer around OpenSSH."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The core idea is simple:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"> **Humans and agents can use a server without needing to know or expose its secret.**"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## What it manages"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"A managed server is more than an IP address."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| Layer | What Hoploom knows |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| **Identity** | alias, hostname, port, username, tags, notes, ProxyJump chain |
| **Credential** | "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"password, private-key reference, key passphrase, ssh-agent/OpenSSH defaults |
| **Context** | workin"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"g paths, host notes, host-bound Agent Skills |
| **Action** | test, connect, execute commands, brows"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"e and transfer files |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"That turns this:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"into this:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"And for an AI agent:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Secrets stay outside the model"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Passwords and key passphrases live in the operating system's native credential vault:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Platform | Secret storage |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| macOS | Keychain |
| Windows | Credential Locker |
| Linux | Secret Service |
| Private keys | Exi"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"sting local file; only the absolute path is stored |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"`hoploom` does **not** inject secrets through command-line arguments, environment variables, config "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"files, or shell history."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Authentication is handled out-of-band through OpenSSH AskPass:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The secret is delivered directly to the SSH authentication process. It is not returned to the caller"},{"id":"p31s2","text":" and does not enter the agent's model context."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Unsafe plaintext keyring backends are rejected rather than silently accepted."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"See the full security model."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Built for AI agents"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"The project ships as an Agent Skill for Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor, and other Agent Skil"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"ls-compatible clients."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"For managed hosts, agents are instructed to use `hoploom` instead of improvising with raw `ssh`, `sc"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"p`, `sftp`, `rsync`, or `sshpass`."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"That gives agents a deterministic, machine-readable interface:"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Connection failures are classified — authentication failure, untrusted host key, timeout, DNS failur"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"e, and more — so an agent can branch on structured results instead of parsing prose."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"### One-line Agent Skill deployment"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"For **DeepSeek Harness**, install the local Hoploom backend below, then run
`dsh plugin --profile we"},{"id":"p41s2","text":"b add dsh-hoploom`. The
dsh plugin supplies inventory/context tools and
explicitly enabled remote op"},{"id":"p41s3","text":"om`. The
dsh plugin supplies inventory/context tools and
explicitly enabled remote operations. 中文说明."},{"id":"p42s1","text":"macOS / Linux:"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"Windows:"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"The installer installs dependencies, exposes `hoploom`, links the skill into detected local agents, "},{"id":"p46s2","text":"and runs `hoploom doctor`."},{"id":"p47s1","text":"Only the CLI and Web UI, without the skill links:"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p49s1","text":"## Host-specific Agent Skills"},{"id":"p50s1","text":"Connecting to a server is only half the problem. After connecting, an agent may also need to know:"},{"id":"p51s1","text":"- cluster topology;
- scheduler conventions;
- approved health checks;
- project directories;
- stor"},{"id":"p51s2","text":"age layouts;
- deployment procedures;
- service-specific runbooks."},{"id":"p52s1","text":"That information should not live in one giant global prompt."},{"id":"p53s1","text":"`Hoploom` lets local Agent Skills be explicitly associated with the hosts where they apply:"},{"id":"p54s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p55s1","text":"The workflow is **target first, context second**:"},{"id":"p56s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p57s1","text":"A host-skill binding is relevance metadata, not authorization. It does not grant permission to opera"},{"id":"p57s2","text":"te on a machine or bypass normal credential and host-key rules."},{"id":"p58s1","text":"Manage bindings explicitly:"},{"id":"p59s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p60s1","text":"When the target changes, agents are expected to resolve again instead of carrying host-specific cont"},{"id":"p60s2","text":"ext across environments."},{"id":"p61s1","text":"See Using Hoploom with AI agents."},{"id":"p62s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p63s1","text":"### From source"},{"id":"p64s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p65s1","text":"Once installed, use `hoploom` directly from PATH."},{"id":"p66s1","text":"### Import the SSH hosts you already have"},{"id":"p67s1","text":"Preview first:"},{"id":"p68s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p69s1","text":"Apply explicitly:"},{"id":"p70s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p71s1","text":"The importer follows OpenSSH `Include` directives and resolves aliases through `ssh -G`. Your origin"},{"id":"p71s2","text":"al `~/.ssh/config` is read but never rewritten."},{"id":"p72s1","text":"### Add a credential"},{"id":"p73s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p74s1","text":"The password is entered through a hidden local prompt and stored in the OS credential vault."},{"id":"p75s1","text":"Private key:"},{"id":"p76s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p77s1","text":"Or use ssh-agent / normal OpenSSH defaults:"},{"id":"p78s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p79s1","text":"There is deliberately no normal CLI command that dumps a stored password back to stdout."},{"id":"p80s1","text":"## What Hoploom is — and is not"}],"truncated":true}
